From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 20:24:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: load descriptors from the constant address space

nir_to_msl emits nir_intrinsic_load_global_constant and
load_global_constant_bounded into MSL's constant address space, but emits
load_global_constant_offset into device. That is the form the descriptor
lowering produces, so every descriptor a shader reads becomes a device load.

A device load cannot be hoisted out of a loop that also stores, because the
compiler has to assume the store aliases it. A shader that loops over a buffer
therefore re-reads the same descriptors every iteration and rebuilds the same
64-bit addresses from them: for dEQP-VK.spirv_assembly.type.vec4.i64
.bit_field_insert_offset8_count8_frag that is five 16-byte loads and about
twenty instructions of address arithmetic per iteration, none of which depend
on the induction variable.

The constant family means memory that cannot change while the shader runs,
which is what the constant address space states, so name it. Atomics keep
device, where the constant space is not addressable.
---
 src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
index a920e1d0375935d395c8a8e79c4ca0d5b6143520..943bdf2d4d8aeb9f4f4d7d60745a111fe03dc1dd 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
@@ -1696,12 +1696,18 @@ intrinsic_to_msl(struct nir_to_msl_ctx *ctx, nir_intrinsic_instr *instr)
    case nir_intrinsic_load_global_constant_offset: {
       enum gl_access_qualifier access = nir_intrinsic_access(instr);
       const char *type = msl_type_for_def(ctx->types, &instr->def);
+      /* The constant load family names memory that cannot change while the
+       * shader runs, and MSL's constant address space says exactly that.
+       * Saying it is what lets the compiler hoist a descriptor load out of a
+       * loop that also stores; from device it has to assume the store aliases.
+       * The sibling load_global_constant and load_global_constant_bounded
+       * already emit constant. */
       const char *addressing =
-         access & ACCESS_COHERENT ? "coherent device" : "device";
+         access & ACCESS_COHERENT ? "coherent device" : "constant";
       if (access & ACCESS_ATOMIC) {
          assert(instr->num_components == 1u &&
                 "We can only do single component with atomics");
-         P(ctx, "atomic_load_explicit((%s atomic_%s*)(", addressing, type);
+         P(ctx, "atomic_load_explicit((device atomic_%s*)(", type);
          src_to_msl(ctx, &instr->src[0]);
          P(ctx, "+");
          src_to_msl(ctx, &instr->src[1]);
